# Port 3000 only

- The only live site is http://localhost:3000/.
- Do not visit, probe, start, restart, or wait for port 4500.
- Do not search for another server or run port-discovery commands.
- Do not restart port 3000 if it is already responding.
- If it stops responding, make one recovery attempt. If that fails, stop and report the error.
- Concept B stays a frozen reference. Read source files or old screenshots. Do not run its server.

# Browser and screenshot review budget

If the user already stated the change, make it. Do not ask them to choose again.

## Tier 0 — no browser

Use no browser actions, refreshes or screenshots for:

- Planning and analysis documents
- Documentation moves
- Copy-only changes
- Source inspection
- Changes limited to font size, weight, colour, line height or letter spacing
- Analysis when the user has already supplied a screenshot

## Tier 1 — ordinary visual edit

For a completed section-level visual edit:

- Implement the full requested change first.
- Perform one browser review only after implementation.
- Refresh once.
- Capture one cropped screenshot of the affected section at 1440×900.
- Do not inspect unrelated sections or produce a full-page screenshot.
- Do not scroll a pinned section to reach the change.
- Stop after the first successful check.

## Tier 2 — responsive or interactive edit

Use this tier only when the request explicitly changes responsive layout, overflow, scrolling, animation or interaction:

- Check 1440px and 390px once each.
- Do not check 1024px unless one of those checks reveals a genuine breakpoint problem or the user explicitly requests it.
- Do not repeat screenshots after a successful result.
- Do not record video or perform a scrolling walkthrough unless explicitly requested.

## General limits

- Reuse screenshots supplied by the user.
- Do not measure every element or inspect DOM geometry unless diagnosing visible clipping, overflow or alignment failure.
- Do not verify that untouched content remains unchanged by taking more screenshots.
- Do not restart an already working server.
- Do not run full builds or full test suites for visual-only edits.
- Run only checks that name the touched files.
- If a command has no useful output for 60 seconds, stop it.
- If verification becomes slow or uncertain, stop and report the specific issue instead of exploring repeatedly.
- Explicit user instructions override the tier limits.
- Report the result and stop.

# Speed budget

- Unless the user explicitly says “verify in browser,” do not open the browser.
- When exact target files are supplied, read and edit only those files and their direct imports.
- Do not reread project documentation for a narrowly scoped edit.
- Do not inspect computed styles, DOM measurements or screenshots unless diagnosing a visible defect.
- When the user can review a local page themselves, provide the URL and stop.
- Never repeat a successful verification.
- If a small task has not produced an edit within three minutes, stop and report the blocker.
- A direct small edit should normally finish without tests, screenshots or browser actions.
